---
/*
 * ONE original drawing (S042, second design read §6.6, 2026-11-14).

 * The read's finding was that the club's own thinking has no visual form: every image on the site is a
 * hundred-year-old printed plate or a Meetup upload, and nothing depicts a thread. This is the one
 * drawing the site owns, drawn in the plates' language rather than borrowed from one: hairlines only,
 * no fills, `currentColor` so the ink is the token rather than a hard-coded hex, and a box that is
 * drawn as a wire through it.

 * The constraints are the ruled ones, and `npm run check:line-art` is the gate that keeps them:
 * under 1200 bytes, strokes only, no fill other than `none`, no colour literal, `role="img"` with an
 * `aria-label` of 12 words or fewer (D324's cap is the alt cap), and a `<figcaption>` carrying the
 * provenance — for an original that means who drew it, not a book citation. No date in the caption:
 * `check:dated-surfaces` rules `/schedule` as the only page that prints a date (D218), and a
 * `2026-11-14` sitting under a drawing on `/chat` reads to a visitor as a meeting date (D325). The
 * day the drawing was made is in this commit's history.

 * Why the thread "Steps you can undo": it is already in `src/content.json`, sourced to the operator
 * (2026-11-03), and its gloss says the thread is "algorithms that lose nothing, drawn as wires and
 * boxes" — the only thread on the list that names a picture. Drawing a different one would be inventing
 * a claim about what the club discusses (D92).
 */
const LABEL = 'A wire running through three boxes, and the same path traced back';
// Round-6 review (2026-11-16), `/chat`/Revise (D412): "The illustration caption: 'drawn for this site in the
// plates' line language: ink hairlines, no fills. Not a scan of a book.' — provenance commentary about your
// own drawing, in a prominent slot. Keep the sentence; demote it to a small caption under the figure."
// It **is** already a small caption under the figure, in `text-micro text-ink-3` - so the demotion the letter
// asks for was already shipped, and what this commit changes is the sentence itself: the quoted thread name
// is deleted, because the list item above the figure already names that thread and the figure's own `aria-label`
// describes it. Repeating a thread title inside a provenance caption is what made the line read as part of the
// list rather than as a credit. `check:line-art` requires a `<figcaption>` with the provenance, and the provenance
// that remains is the whole of what a reader needs to know about a drawing the site owns: it is the site's own.
const CAPTION = 'Drawn for this site in the plates\u2019 line language: ink hairlines, no fills, not a scan of a book.';
---

<figure data-line-art="undoable-steps" class="mt-3">
  {/* `check:line-art` measures the figure's BYTES in the emitted page (622 against a 1200 cap
     @measured 2026-11-14), and Astro does not render a brace-comment, so a note inside the drawing costs
     nothing against that cap — it is here because a nine-path wire is hard to read without one. The
     reasoning for each stroke lives here and in the frontmatter note:
     the forward wire is broken where a box interrupts it, and each span is a cubic rather than a dead
     straight line — the wobble is the drawing's personality and it costs about 60 bytes. The return path
     comes over the top so the reader sees one closed circuit rather than two separate drawings. */}
  <svg viewBox="0 0 240 96" role="img" aria-label={LABEL} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
    <path d="M6 52c13-1 20 1 30 0" />
    <path d="M70 52c11 1 18-1 24 0" />
    <path d="M128 52c11-1 19 1 24 0" />
    <path d="M186 52c15 1 24-1 28 0" />
    <rect x="36" y="34" width="34" height="36" />
    <rect x="94" y="34" width="34" height="36" />
    <rect x="152" y="34" width="34" height="36" />
    {/* The return path: the same three boxes, traversed the other way, which is what "undoable" means.
        It comes back over the top so the reader sees one closed circuit, not two separate drawings. */}
    <path d="M220 44c5-13-9-21-22-21H26c-13 0-20 8-20 21" />
    <path d="M6 44l4 8 7-5" />
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="mt-2 text-micro leading-prose text-ink-3 font-body">{CAPTION}</figcaption>
</figure>
